7","id":2799022959,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6m1bNv","user":{"login":"CrayolaEater","id":38570835,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTcwODM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38570835?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CrayolaEater","html_url":"https://github.com/CrayolaEater","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CrayolaEater/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CrayolaEater/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CrayolaEater/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CrayolaEater/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CrayolaEater/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CrayolaEater/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CrayolaEater/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CrayolaEater/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CrayolaEater/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-12T20:10:57Z","updated_at":"2025-04-12T20:10:57Z","body":"> I'm not a big fan of random APIs that don't involve an explicit generator (using a global one instead). But i guess the analogue in Array already exists?\r\n\r\nthats literally how Array does it ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2799022959/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2799852763","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105317#issuecomment-2799852763","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105317","id":2799852763,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6m4lzb","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-13T08:11:12Z","updated_at":"2025-04-13T08:12:18Z","body":"Sorry, i didn't mean to criticize your approach :) if Array offers the same method, it does make sense for packed arrays to do so too to have API consistency.\nI'm just personally not a fan of this API style in general, and would rather like to see Random APIs expanded to deal with different kinds of arrays than arrays expanded to deal more with randomness. I should probably have worded that better.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2799852763/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2799886619","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105317#issuecomment-2799886619","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105317","id":2799886619,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6m4uEb","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-13T09:56:30Z","updated_at":"2025-04-13T10:17:02Z","body":"I feel like this warrants a feature proposal.\r\nNot to say it's not useful, but I do not agree that this method is particularly needed for the other array types.\r\n\r\nAt the end of the day, this method is a shorthand for a very simple operation, which can be replicated with corresponding methods in both the global scope and the **RandomNumberGenerator** class. It likely should be replicated for more advanced cases, too, as users would be inclined to have more control over it.\r\n**Array** itself at least _somewhat_ warrants it, as the simplest array in Godot that users can interact with, and the type with the most utility methods associated to it.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2799886619/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2799976078","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105317#issu